+### Eviction policy (2Q)
+
+The cache replaces entries with a two-queue policy that separates sheets seen once from sheets that are reused. Two queues hold cached entries:
+
+- **Probation queue** — a sheet enters here when it is first admitted after rendering. Entries are ordered oldest-first.
+- **Protected queue** — a cache hit on a sheet while it is in the probation queue promotes that sheet here. A hit on a sheet already in the protected queue refreshes its position. Entries are ordered least-recently-used first.
+
+When admitting a completed sheet would exceed the 12 GiB bound, the worker evicts from the probation queue oldest-first, and only when the probation queue cannot supply enough space does it evict from the protected queue least-recently-used first. A long sequential screening therefore cycles through the probation queue and evicts its own one-use sheets before any reused comparison sheet is touched.
+
+The probation and protected queues partition the 12 GiB budget; the split is a worker-internal parameter left to tuning (see Open Questions). The policy reads and updates only its own queues and exposes no counters, queue membership, or size split to the review API or to clients. It does not change the HTTP interface, the render queue's four-job concurrency, or the 12 GiB disk budget.
+
+## Decisions & Alternatives
+
+| Decision | Chosen | Alternatives Considered | Rationale |
+|----------|--------|------------------------|-----------|
+| Cache eviction policy | 2Q, with probation and protected queues ([decision](decisions/eviction-policy.md)) | LRU; frequency-based eviction with aging | Protects reused comparison sheets from eviction during long sequential screenings, which stream many one-use sheets through the cache. LRU needs little bookkeeping and follows recent work quickly but lets a screening scan evict comparison sheets. Aged frequency counts retain repeatedly popular clips but add counter maintenance and can keep yesterday's favorites across a project switch. 2Q's two-queue split adds bookkeeping and a tunable size parameter, carried entirely inside the worker's private cache. |
+
+## Open Questions & Future Decisions
+
+### Resolved
+
+1. ✅ Cache eviction policy selected (2Q); see Decisions & Alternatives.
+
+### Deferred
+
+1. Probation/protected queue size split — the tuning parameter; no default set.
+2. Admission of a sheet that alone exceeds the probation queue's share of the budget.
+3. Eviction ordering when admitting one sheet requires evicting entries from both queues.
